1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:27,480
Oh, hey. Did Rishi tell you about his spear? There's like a whole story.

2
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:31,020
He sure did. Talk about a real tearjerker, am I right?

3
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:35,000
Yeah, it was sad. I really hope he's doing okay out there.

4
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:40,160
I recently began work on my superb rebranding plan.

5
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:46,080
I'll write a book about their past. I'll spread the plain truth about their curse and persecution.

6
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,220
But I haven't figured out how I want to present it.

7
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:56,160
A documentary approach? Diary style? I don't think I could handle a whole odyssey.

8
00:00:56,160 --> 00:01:02,380
How about a simple booklet? Say, ten pages. Packaged with a figure.

9
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:07,180
So, what are you working on?

10
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:14,060
I'm trying to write a book about Rishiard's past. His heroic exploits.

11
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,500
Is that all you have so far?

12
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:19,500
Yeah. I'm just getting started.

13
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,740
Um, I want to help. If you don't think I'd get in the way.

14
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:24,480
Huh?

15
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,000
Rishiard told me a lot about his past while we were traveling here together.

16
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,540
I think I could probably write some good stories.

17
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:35,780
Yeah? I'd love that. Although, I still want your classes to come first.

18
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:37,800
Okay.

19
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,200
Bye.

20
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:48,820
Bye.

21
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:48,980
Bye.

22
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:49,740
Bye.

23
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:50,840
Bye.

24
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:50,980
Bye.

25
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:51,560
Bye.

26
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,060
Bye.

27
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:52,820
Bye.

28
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:52,960
Bye.

29
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:54,900
Bye.

30
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:56,960
Bye.

31
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:57,560
Bye.

32
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:01,780
Bye.

33
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:02,860
Bye.

34
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:03,740
Bye.

35
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,060
Bye.

36
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:04,740
Bye.

37
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:05,900
Bye.

38
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:06,480
Bye.

39
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,580
Bye.

40
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:23,300
Aisha, if there's something on your mind, you know you can tell me, right?

41
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:26,240
What does that mean? I'm fine.

42
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:30,580
Just if you think I'm spending too much time with Norn and you want to hang out more together,

43
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:34,020
or if you're feeling overwhelmed and want to break from work.

44
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:34,580
Hmm.

45
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,100
Well, if I may.

46
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:40,960
I would like a salary, please.

47
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,780
Thank you, miss.

48
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,560
What do you want those for?

49
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:51,760
I collected a bunch of different flower seeds on our trip up here, so now I'd like to try and grow them.

50
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,380
Would that be okay?

51
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:55,640
Absolutely.

52
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:59,440
Although, maybe we should pick up some potting soil, too.

53
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:01,940
The earth around here doesn't seem the most fertile.

54
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:06,780
I was actually going to ask if you would make some for me yourself with your incredible earth magic.

55
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,360
Would that be okay?

56
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:09,660
Absolutely.

57
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:10,940
Thanks, Rudeus.

58
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,160
Pretty.

59
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,440
Are you getting those as a present for Sylphie?

60
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:22,320
Yep.

61
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,880
I'm the kind of guy who wants to treat his wife right.

62
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,640
Sylphie's a very lucky woman to have you.

63
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,060
Oh, that big brother.

64
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:32,900
I do hope you'll try to spare some of that love from me every once in a while.

65
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,060
Absolutely not.

66
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:35,480
Not that kind of love.

67
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:36,220
Oh.

68
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:40,320
I can't give you a better deal than this.

69
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,060
Come on, just a little bit lower.

70
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:47,720
If it helps you to know my older brother here is Rudeus Greyrat, the university's famous mage.

71
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:48,040
Huh?

72
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,660
And between us.

73
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:50,960
You know Princess Ariel?

74
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,800
She respects my brother and they even work together.

75
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,640
Greyrat, you say?

76
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,660
And the princess would approve.

77
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,840
I guess I could.

78
00:04:59,340 --> 00:04:59,920
All right.

79
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:00,840
You got a deal.

80
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:01,860
Yes!

81
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:05,160
You know I don't mind chipping in a little bit if you're short.

82
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,080
Mm-mm.

83
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,120
Not to worry.

84
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,520
I have just enough.

85
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:10,880
See?

86
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,640
Wow, talk about business sense.

87
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,700
That's kind of intimidating.

88
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:20,880
I've always wanted to own some cute decor like this.

89
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:23,320
Lilia didn't get stuff like that for you and Millis?

90
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:25,340
No, she considered it disrespectful.

91
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:28,900
She said a maid shouldn't buy furnishings to suit her own taste.

92
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:33,720
But you're okay with it?

93
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:36,380
Absolutely.

94
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:48,320
Next, we'll focus on summoning organic matter from our old world.

95
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,160
Organic?

96
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,180
Yes.

97
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,660
Hopefully food.

98
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:58,680
Is the step with the detailed conditions really necessary?

99
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,560
Yes.

100
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:03,880
I don't want to teleport myself back to a foreign country or the middle of the ocean.

101
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,080
Right, that makes sense.

102
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:10,240
So she'll get closer and closer to summoning something as complex as a human being,

103
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:13,580
then teleport herself back to Japan with pinpoint accuracy.

104
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:18,400
Defining the conditions can be tricky, so I'll need to visit the old man again for that.

105
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,600
The mysterious summoning authority you vaguely mentioned?

106
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:22,260
Yeah.

107
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,400
Now, not to change the subject or anything,

108
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:28,180
but here, your reward for the bottle.

109
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:29,500
What is it?

110
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:32,020
A summoning scroll for a lamplight spirit.

111
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:35,980
It will float along behind the caster, emitting a bright light.

112
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,160
Though, it will fade as its mana dwindles.

113
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,200
That's an original.

114
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,000
The old man designed it himself,

115
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:45,320
and not even the Mage's Guild has access to it.

116
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:49,520
What Japanese guy doesn't go nuts for limited editions?

117
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:52,940
And if our next experiment succeeds,

118
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,540
I'll give you something even better.

119
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,880
So please, I'm counting on your help.

120
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,500
Zanoba, meanwhile, finally finished making a figure with his own hands,

121
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,160
and gave it to Julie as a gift.

122
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,060
Thanks, Master.

123
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,780
You was welcome, Master.

124
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,660
I will cherish this forever.

125
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:16,820
You're very welcome.

126
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,240
Keep up the good work.

127
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:19,600
Okay.

128
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,420
Man.

129
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,960
Zanoba giving away a figure.

130
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,300
Isn't that nice, Julie?

131
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,260
You take good care of it now.

132
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,540
After helping Rue Jird bring my sisters here,

133
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:32,620
Ginger chose to go back to work for Zanoba.

134
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,300
A decision which I can't say I understand.

135
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:38,380
But she's also been teaching Julie etiquette.

136
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:42,040
She's helped her make huge strides in speaking the human tongue as well.

137
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:45,480
And she says she rented a room near the school,

138
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:48,240
which makes her sound more like a commuter wife than a knight.

139
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:50,380
What do you need?

140
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:51,280
Nothing.

141
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:55,360
I guess I was just wondering what made you pledge your fealty to Zanoba.

142
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:59,380
Because Prince Zanoba's mother asked me to.

143
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,820
She personally entrusted his care to me.

144
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:04,180
I devoted myself to him then and there.

145
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:07,000
I swore I would serve him until my dying breath.

146
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:07,860
Wow.

147
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,300
That sounds like a really moving story.

148
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:11,860
Then what?

149
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,000
That's all there is.

150
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,360
I don't have any subordinates.

151
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,900
Ginger was my last guard, but I traded her to Pax for the Roxy figure.

152
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:23,520
What a fantastic bargain that was.

153
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:27,220
How can she stay loyal to him after he treated her like that?

154
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:30,840
I guess families do come in all shapes and sizes.

155
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:35,120
I haven't found a full cure yet.

156
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:37,740
Only this method of suppression.

157
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:42,960
This prototype can force in external mana, counter to the flow of her internal mana.

158
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:47,380
So at the very least, it can relieve Alina Lisa's symptoms.

159
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:50,000
But there are two major problems.

160
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:50,860
That's not bad.

161
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:55,000
I guess the first problem is it's horrible.

162
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,220
Indeed it is.

163
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:57,620
I wouldn't wear it.

164
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:02,120
But I do believe with Zonaba and Silent's help, I can at least make it smaller.

165
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:04,340
Then what's the second problem?

166
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:07,800
Even for a prototype, it drains far too much mana.

167
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,020
It only lasts an hour.

168
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,640
Lisa can't recharge it at all without me.

169
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:18,600
And since that limits us to conducting only a few tests a day, I thought to call you.

170
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,240
Would you mind charging it?

171
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,200
Yeah, of course.

172
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:22,640
I'm always happy to help.

173
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:23,920
I appreciate that.

174
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:28,740
So Cliff is making slow but steady progress toward his goals too.

175
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,000
Good.

176
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:31,340
Good for him.

177
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:38,940
I'd say I've found a really nice rhythm lately.

178
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:41,080
I work out.

179
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,000
I eat breakfast.

180
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:47,500
I go to school, see friends, check in on how everyone's research is going.

181
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:50,140
I help Norn study.

182
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:52,880
Then go home for some family time.

183
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,200
Every day looks about the same, but I'm still making progress step by step.

184
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,400
I never managed anything like this last time.

185
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:06,180
I think this is what you call real happiness.

186
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,300
I need a bath.

187
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,520
What are you doing up?

188
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:22,560
It's still so early.

189
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:23,780
Oh gosh.

190
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:28,480
Now that it's time, I'm kind of starting to get cold feet.

191
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:29,940
You have nothing to be afraid of.

192
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,160
You can do it, Sophie.

193
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:32,720
Show some courage.

194
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:44,500
Rudy, you should know, I haven't had a you-know-what in two months.

195
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:51,040
And, well, I haven't been feeling so great lately, so I was starting to wonder.

196
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:56,460
Anyway, Aisha went with me to see the neighborhood doctor.

197
00:10:56,460 --> 00:11:02,560
And, um, turns out that I'm probably expecting.

198
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,840
Is that okay?

199
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:11,420
Say something.

200
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,100
Is it okay if I feel?

201
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:14,940
Huh?

202
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:16,520
Oh, of course.

203
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:17,420
Go right ahead.

204
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:28,200
Brother dear, don't you have anything to say?

205
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,040
Your wife is waiting for you.

206
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:50,480
Thank you.

207
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:51,740
I love you.

208
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:52,320
What?

209
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,660
Why are you thanking me?

210
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:54,440
Sorry.

211
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:55,860
I just...

212
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:56,480
I don't know.

213
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,080
I can't find the words.

214
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:05,580
Rudy, you wanted kids pretty badly, didn't you?

215
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:23,780
Ahem.

216
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,220
Big brother.

217
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:29,220
Your wife is in a delicate condition, so for the time being...

218
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:31,560
All right.

219
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,980
Wow, I'm gonna be an aunt, huh?

220
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:37,960
Congratulations!

221
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:40,000
Aunt Norn, I like that.

222
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:45,380
Princess Ariel indicated that Miss Sylphia's relief from her duties for at least two years.

223
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:50,480
And while you're on family leave, great Aunt Alina Lise will assume your bodyguard duties.

224
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:51,860
You'll need the time off.

225
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,060
Is Grandma going to be okay with that?

226
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,660
She's still got her curse.

227
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,580
She personally assured me she could manage.

228
00:12:58,800 --> 00:12:59,620
I wouldn't worry.

229
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:02,400
I informed the rest of your circle as well.

230
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,240
They're happy for you both.

231
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:06,220
They promised me they'd check on you.

232
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:06,880
They did?

233
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,360
Thank you, Aisha.

234
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,120
Oh, any time, brother dear.

235
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,700
Thanks for this meal.

236
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:18,300
I was thinking.

237
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:22,180
Dad is probably gonna be shocked when he shows up and finds out he's a grandpa.

238
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,600
Oh yeah, he'll be so surprised.

239
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:25,620
That's for sure.

240
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:26,520
Yeah.

241
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:29,140
Guys like him love to spoil their grandchildren.

242
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,320
He'll be happy.

243
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,980
I'll never forget how over the moon he was when you two were born.

244
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:35,480
That's our daddy.

245
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:36,960
I can't wait.

246
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:46,020
Sylphia and I got married and our whole family will be here.

247
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,780
The paradise I dreamed of back in Buena Village is almost a reality.

248
00:13:50,780 --> 00:14:08,520
Zenith Rescue in dire state.

249
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,220
Send help immediately.

250
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:19,020
Hi!

251
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:20,360
Oh, great.

252
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:21,560
What's going on?

253
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:22,500
What do you mean?

254
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:23,700
The letter from Geese.

255
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:27,140
He said they're having trouble rescuing Zenith and that they need help.

256
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,120
You're not wrong.

257
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:30,780
Sounds like trouble indeed.

258
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:31,660
You think?

259
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:32,720
Come on!

260
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,900
You told me I'd regret going to Begarit.

261
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,320
Why did you trick me?

262
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:37,480
Trick you?

263
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,480
No, no, no.

264
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:41,840
If you go to Begarit, you will regret it.

265
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,540
That much has not changed.

266
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,120
Ah, okay.

267
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,140
I see.

268
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:47,860
That's how this plays out.

269
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:50,200
What you're trying to tell me here is...

270
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,320
I'm gonna regret it if I go to Begarit.

271
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,720
Also, I'll regret not going.

272
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:55,400
That right?

273
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,380
No, it's not like that.

274
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,380
Think about it.

275
00:14:58,380 --> 00:15:00,260
Did you regret it until yesterday?

276
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,300
You made lots of friends.

277
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:06,200
You met all sorts of people and did a bit of growing yourself.

278
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:10,260
Your condition was cured and you made up with your sisters.

279
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:12,160
Also...

280
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:14,180
You got married and now you're a papa.

281
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:17,480
Sure, it hasn't been bad.

282
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:18,460
I'll admit it.

283
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,280
But still, it's wrong.

284
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,000
You lied.

285
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,880
You said I shouldn't go to Begarit.

286
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:25,020
You tricked me.

287
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,560
Take it easy.

288
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,120
There's no trick.

289
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,700
In fact, I'll tell you what I told you then.

290
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,360
Steer clear of the Begarit continent.

291
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,320
You'll regret going there.

292
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,760
Enough of this crap.

293
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:38,200
My family's in trouble.

294
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,340
At least tell me why I'll regret it.

295
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,140
My lips are sealed.

296
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:43,920
Damn it!

297
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:47,160
How could I forget that you're nothing but a giant asshole?

298
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:49,080
What a harsh thing to say.

299
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:51,740
My advice has always been rather helpful, no?

300
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:52,960
So what if it has?

301
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:55,220
That doesn't change the fact that you tricked me.

302
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:58,560
Please, just give me a hint of something I can use here.

303
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:00,520
What am I gonna regret, huh?

304
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:01,740
Tell me!

305
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,300
How do I make a choice like this without any info?

306
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,160
What does anyone do?

307
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:08,360
Most people make their decisions in the dark.

308
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:09,940
You sound so greedy.

309
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:11,960
I'm greedy, is that it?

310
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,000
Well, I don't want any regrets!

311
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,920
If you think about it, it's quite obvious.

312
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:21,180
You've spent a year and a half in Magic University.

313
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:24,380
Your sisters took approximately one year to reach you.

314
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:27,360
If you had gone to Begarit, you would have missed them.

315
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,520
Not true.

316
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,240
My sisters only came to me because Paul got my letter.

317
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,480
If I'd never sent it to him, they would have stayed put.

318
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,720
Either in Millis or that port town.

319
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:37,880
Think!

320
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:41,960
If you hadn't written your letter, Paul would have sent them to the Kingdom of Asura.

321
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,720
Lilia's got family there, don't you remember?

322
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:46,080
Fair point.

323
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:48,100
You're probably right about that.

324
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,580
It's the same now.

325
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:50,920
You have a wife.

326
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,280
You leave her and the child, and then?

327
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,860
What happens when you're traveling to Begarit?

328
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:59,820
Do you plan on leaving your family alone while you hike across the world?

329
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:02,420
I see.

330
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,400
I can't avoid regrets.

331
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:05,420
That's the deal.

332
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,160
Right.

333
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:09,460
Regret is inevitable, no matter how hard you try.

334
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:13,080
If you go to Begarit, you'll miss out on a great opportunity.

335
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,760
So I suggest that you stay.

336
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:21,780
Well, if you're this adamant, then sounds like there's only one choice.

337
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:22,820
Final stay.

338
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:23,860
Really?

339
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,200
Great!

340
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,440
You want some advice?

341
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:27,540
Sure.

342
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,400
How much worse could it get?

343
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,880
Rudeus, stay home until next mating season.

344
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:38,820
When it comes, Lidia and Persina will pounce at you relentlessly.

345
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:41,640
You shall choose to have relations with one of them.

346
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:46,800
And if you do this, your life will be filled with even greater happiness in the end.

347
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,960
Now you want me to cheat on my wife?

348
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:50,360
I've already made up my mind.

349
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,800
Sylvie is the only one.

350
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:53,760
And the girls and I are just friends.

351
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:55,080
It's not like that, damn it!

352
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,580
Rudy, are you okay?

353
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,000
Was it a nightmare?

354
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:09,500
I'm okay.

355
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,360
Lidia and Persina aside, the man-god had a point.

356
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:19,580
No matter how hard I think about a decision, I can never be certain about the outcome.

357
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:23,360
I can only be certain about one thing.

358
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:26,440
It'll take me at least a year to reach Begarit.

359
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,220
It's that letter.

360
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,300
You can't seem to get it off your mind.

361
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:33,080
Listen, Rudy.

362
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:34,960
It's not just you.

363
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:37,000
Your sisters are concerned as well.

364
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,060
But please don't worry about me.

365
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:40,100
I'll be fine, okay?

366
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:46,540
I'm not going.

367
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:48,960
I'll stay with you.

368
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:56,720
Send help immediately.

369
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,940
I wonder what went wrong.

370
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:02,000
The letter did come from Geese, not Paul.

371
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:06,140
Maybe he sent it in a moment of panic before he met up with Paul's group.

372
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:09,060
They might have rescued Zenith already.

373
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,060
If I go now, there's a chance I could miss them.

374
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:16,140
But what if...

375
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:21,480
Wise choice, Rudeus.

376
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:23,760
You're better off staying behind for this one.

377
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,080
So that's how it is.

378
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:25,760
You're going?

379
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:27,300
You sure you should?

380
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:31,000
As Sylphie's grandmother, I'd like to do something to help her family.

381
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,980
That's noble, but what about poor Cliff?

382
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:35,680
I'll break up with him.

383
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:37,340
What else can I do?

384
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,140
He'll wait for you if you explain yourself.

385
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:43,840
Yes, but that boy has the makings of a future Pope.

386
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,480
It would be selfish of me to hold him back.

387
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:50,480
He's better off remembering me as a youthful indiscretion.

388
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:53,480
Leaving it at that will be the best thing for his career.

389
00:19:58,300 --> 00:19:59,680
Ah, yes, I see.

390
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:03,900
I'm sure you'll deal with this matter easily enough and be back before too long.

391
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:09,300
I will remain here and continue to pursue my research, but I will be praying for your speedy return.

392
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,780
I kind of thought you'd ask me not to go or demand to join.

393
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:17,180
Should you wish for me to accompany you, Master, I would be loathe to refuse.

394
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:22,160
But being unaccustomed to lengthy journeys, I fear I might prove to be a burden.

395
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:26,980
Besides, I could hardly imagine taking Julie on such a long trek.

396
00:20:26,980 --> 00:20:30,160
Well, what about me?

397
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:32,080
You think I should go?

398
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,660
That's for you to decide, Master.

399
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:39,880
If I may, allow me to offer one piece of advice.

400
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:45,600
A child never stops growing, with or without their father.

401
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,140
If you're worried about your parents, I suggest you go.

402
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:52,960
I'll guarantee the safety of your wife and sisters in your absence.

403
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:57,980
Although, if it were up to me, of course, I'd never want to leave your side.

404
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,020
That means a lot.

405
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:18,260
Sylphie won't be alone.

406
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:20,260
My sisters are here with her.

407
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:22,820
She'll do just fine without me.

408
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:32,800
And yet, I still feel torn as the pillar of this family.

409
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:38,260
As a husband and a father, I have a duty to stay by their side.

410
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:40,520
They're my world now.

411
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:42,620
I can't just leave them like this.

412
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:59,400
Where are you going, Norn?

413
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:03,800
Norn!

414
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:09,720
Hey, are you okay?

415
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:16,380
I just thought, if you won't go, I guess it's up to me then.

416
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,960
Oh, Norn, you won't make it.

417
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:20,980
But, Rudius, please.

418
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:22,960
Mom and Ted are in trouble.

419
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,660
They need our help.

420
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:27,260
So why?

421
00:22:27,540 --> 00:22:28,360
Tell me!

422
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:30,800
Why are you going to help them, big brother?

423
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,260
Just go!

424
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:33,740
You're so much stronger!

425
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,060
And you're fit to travel, so...

426
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:36,880
Why not?

427
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:38,000
Rudy!

428
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,720
She's right.

429
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,300
I can do it.

430
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:48,440
Unlike me, she can't go, no matter how much she wants to.

431
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:51,720
But me...

432
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:54,280
I can.

433
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:02,640
Hey, Norn.

434
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:07,460
I'll go find them.

435
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,920
Will you watch the house while I'm gone?

436
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:14,600
Yes.

437
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,720
Please don't fight with your sister.

438
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:19,340
And help out Sylphie when you can, okay?

439
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:20,580
Okay.

440
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:22,620
All right.

441
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:23,700
Good girl.

442
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:25,780
Please help them.

443
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:27,120
For me.

444
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:29,640
For us.

445
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:32,040
I'm going to save our family.

